# How fast a clip plays against the game's ticks, running and frozen-stepped (the Motion Studio, phase 2, 2026-11-25):
# the same trotting lioness recorded first with the game running (several moments a tick), then frozen and stepped a
# tick a picture as every frame film does. Each moment's clip time (play.body[1]) against its tick shows whether the
# clip moves its play speed in clip ticks a game tick in both.
#   ./gradlew runFilm -PfilmScene=tools/film/clip_clock.film     then read run-film/screenshots/clip_clock/body.jsonl.gz
scene clip_clock
cmd time set noon
cmd weather clear
lens 50
cmd fill -30 -61 -7 30 -50 7 minecraft:air
cmd fill -30 -63 -7 30 -63 7 minecraft:dirt
cmd fill -30 -62 -7 30 -62 7 minecraft:grass_block
wait 20
walker antcolonies:lioness -20.5 -61 0.5 -90
aim film-walker
cam side 0 1.2 -7
go 16 -61 0 1.27
record on 6 all
cmd tick unfreeze
wait 40
cmd tick freeze
burst stepped 20 1
record off
cam off
cmd tick unfreeze
